<h1 class="chapter-title">CHAPTER 3: REQUIREMENTS ANALYSIS & FEASIBILITY STUDY</h1>

<h3 class="subsection-title">3.1 Stakeholder Personas</h3>
1. <strong>Blind / Visually Impaired Examinee (Student):</strong> Requires complete auditory independence, zero mouse dependency, clear high-contrast visual cues for low-vision individuals, and voice-guided question narration and answer dictation.
2. <strong>Educator / Faculty Proctor (Teacher):</strong> Requires rapid exam creation, question paper uploading, live proctoring telemetry monitoring, and evaluation tools.
3. <strong>Institutional Administrator:</strong> Requires full platform governance, student/teacher account authorization, support inquiry resolution, and automated database backups.

<h3 class="subsection-title">3.2 Functional Requirements Specifications (FRS)</h3>

<table class="academic-table">
<thead><tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Module</th><th>Functional Description</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>FR01</strong></td><td>Voice Assistant</td><td>System shall activate speech recognition when user taps anywhere across the screen.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR02</strong></td><td>Speech Navigation</td><td>System shall parse natural voice commands (e.g., "Student Login", "Take Exam") and route to routes.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR03</strong></td><td>Exam Narration</td><td>System shall sequentially read question numbers, question text, and instructions via TTS.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR04</strong></td><td>Voice Dictation</td><td>System shall convert the examinee's spoken response into text and display it inside the answer box.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR05</strong></td><td>Face Registration</td><td>System shall capture and verify the student's facial profile via webcam before unlocking exam.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR06</strong></td><td>Absence Detection</td><td>System shall trigger audio-visual warnings if the student's face is absent for more than 5 seconds.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR07</strong></td><td>Intruder Detection</td><td>System shall detect unauthorized second/third persons in the camera frame immediately.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR08</strong></td><td>Violation Lockout</td><td>System shall issue Warning 1 on first violation, Warning 2 on second, and <strong>auto-terminate on 3rd</strong>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR09</strong></td><td>Emergency SOS</td><td>System shall permit students to trigger SOS alerts that appear instantly on teacher dashboards.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR10</strong></td><td>Contact Support</td><td>Users can submit inquiries via Contact Us, which appear dynamically on the Admin Dashboard.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR11</strong></td><td>Admin Governance</td><td>Administrator can view telemetry, manage users, and export full platform backups as JSON.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>FR12</strong></td><td>Auth & Recovery</td><td>System enforces alphanumeric passwords and provides 2-step OTP email recovery.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h3 class="subsection-title">3.3 Non-Functional Requirements Specifications (NFRS)</h3>
- <strong>NFR01 (Usability & WCAG Conformance):</strong> Strict compliance with WCAG 2.1 AA standards; color contrast ratio $\ge 7:1$ in high-contrast mode; all buttons must have descriptive ARIA labels.
- <strong>NFR02 (Latency & Responsiveness):</strong> Speech recognition response latency shall not exceed 350ms; video frame inference shall achieve at least 15 FPS on standard consumer webcams.
- <strong>NFR03 (Reliability & Fault Tolerance):</strong> If MongoDB disconnects or cloud latency spikes, client-side fallback stores (`localStorage` and in-memory caches) shall maintain uninterrupted exam sessions.
- <strong>NFR04 (Security & Data Integrity):</strong> Password hashes must be salted and encrypted using bcrypt; REST endpoints protected by JWT session verification.
- <strong>NFR05 (Cross-Platform Browser Compatibility):</strong> Seamless execution across Google Chrome 90+, Microsoft Edge 90+, Mozilla Firefox 88+, and Apple Safari 14+.

<h3 class="subsection-title">3.4 Hardware Requirements</h3>
- <strong>Client (Student / Teacher / Admin Workstation):</strong>
  - Processor: Intel Core i3 / AMD Ryzen 3 (or equivalent) $\ge 2.0\text{ GHz}$.
  - Memory: 4 GB RAM minimum (8 GB recommended for optimal multi-tab computer vision).
  - Webcam: Standard integrated or external USB camera ($720\text{p} @ 30\text{ FPS}$).
  - Audio: Integrated microphone and stereo speakers / headphones.
- <strong>Server / Deployment Infrastructure:</strong>
  - Node.js runtime environment (v18.x or v20.x LTS).
  - MongoDB Atlas Cloud Database cluster (M0 / M2 tier).
  - Vercel Serverless Edge runtime with global CDN caching.

<h3 class="subsection-title">3.5 Software Stack Specifications</h3>
- <strong>Client Frontend:</strong> React 18.2.0, Vite 5.4, Lucide-React 0.344, W3C Web Speech API.
- <strong>Backend API:</strong> Node.js, Express 4.19, Mongoose 8.2, Nodemailer 6.9, CORS, Dotenv.
- <strong>Styling:</strong> Modular CSS-in-JS inline responsive styles with high-contrast amber/navy palette.

