<h1 class="chapter-title">CHAPTER 5: SYSTEM METHODOLOGY & MODULE IMPLEMENTATION</h1>

<h3 class="subsection-title">5.1 Hands-Free Voice Navigation Pipeline</h3>
Traditional web navigation relies on visual saccades and mouse-driven pointer clicks. For visually impaired individuals, interacting with a screen requires auditory mapping. VisionAssist AI introduces a two-tier voice interaction model:
1. <strong>Viewport Touch Interaction:</strong> The entire viewport acts as an omnidirectional tactile switch. Clicking or tapping anywhere on the screen stops ongoing speech and initiates speech recognition.
2. <strong>Intent Parsing & Dispatch:</strong> The voice recognizer converts spoken speech to a normalized string and executes a rule-based parser that handles navigation keywords ("student login", "teacher dashboard", "take exam", "instructions", "help") and triggers navigation without sighted assistance.

<h3 class="subsection-title">5.2 Accessible Computer-Based Examination Pipeline</h3>
The student examination module ([`StudentDashboard.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/NAYANA%20N%20S/Desktop/ai-blind-assistant-01/Frontend/src/components/StudentDashboard.jsx)) follows a structured, voice-guided procedure:
1. <strong>Question Narration:</strong> The system invokes speech synthesis to read the question number and text clearly.
2. <strong>Audio Dictation:</strong> When the student speaks their response, the Web Speech Recognition API streams transcripts in real time into the answer text area.
3. <strong>Auditory Readback & Review:</strong> The examinee can ask the system to read back their current answer for verification before proceeding to the next question.
4. <strong>Automated Submission:</strong> When the countdown timer expires, the exam engine halts speech input and submits all responses to `/api/student-exams/submit`.

<h3 class="subsection-title">5.3 AI Proctoring & Multi-Person Intruder Detection Pipeline</h3>
Academic integrity during unproctored remote examinations is maintained by the AI Proctoring Engine. The engine functions as an automated state machine running directly in the browser:
1. <strong>Face Registration:</strong> Upon clicking "Start Exam", the webcam captures the examinee's reference face coordinates and geometry.
2. <strong>Continuous Frame Processing:</strong> The webcam video feed is sampled continuously to evaluate two key conditions:
   - <strong>Condition A (Face Absence):</strong> If zero faces are detected, an absence timer begins. If the face remains undetected for longer than the tolerance threshold (5 seconds), a violation event is recorded.
   - <strong>Condition B (Multi-Person Intrusion):</strong> If two or more distinct faces appear within the video frame, a multi-person violation is triggered.
3. <strong>Enforcement State Machine:</strong>
   - <strong>Initial State:</strong> Status is `Normal` (Green indicator).
   - <strong>Violation 1:</strong> Audio warning plays: <em>"Warning 1! Multiple people or absence detected. Return to your seat."</em> (Warning 1 recorded).
   - <strong>Violation 2:</strong> Loud alert plays: <em>"Warning 2! Final notice. Another violation will terminate your exam."</em> (Warning 2 recorded).
   - <strong>Violation 3:</strong> Exam is automatically terminated and submitted with a disqualified status.

<h3 class="subsection-title">5.4 Educator / Teacher Assessment Hub</h3>
Educators access a purpose-built portal ([`TeacherDashboard.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/NAYANA%20N%20S/Desktop/ai-blind-assistant-01/Frontend/src/components/TeacherDashboard.jsx)) containing:
- <strong>Exam Builder:</strong> Create accessible tests with customized durations and marking schemes.
- <strong>Live SOS Rescue Monitor:</strong> Receives instantaneous emergency alerts from students with direct voice-response or text-dispatch capabilities.
- <strong>Proctoring Audit Log:</strong> Displays chronological violation logs with timestamps and violation types.

<h3 class="subsection-title">5.5 Administrator Platform Governance & Support Ticket Hub</h3>
The Administrator Dashboard ([`AdminDashboard.jsx`](file:///c:/Users/NAYANA%20N%20S/Desktop/ai-blind-assistant-01/Frontend/src/components/AdminDashboard.jsx)) provides central control over the system:
- <strong>Live User Directory:</strong> Real-time visibility into registered and currently logged-in students and faculty.
- <strong>Support & Inquiries Desk:</strong> Centralized inbox displaying all messages submitted through the Contact Us modal, complete with unread counter badges, status toggles, and direct email reply integrations.
- <strong>System Settings Hub:</strong> Configures platform identity, AI speech engine parameters, proctoring warning limits, and database backup exports (.JSON format).

