<h1 class="chapter-title">CHAPTER 8: RESULTS, PERFORMANCE EVALUATION & DISCUSSION</h1>

<h3 class="subsection-title">8.1 Performance Benchmarks</h3>
Quantitative performance benchmarks were measured over 100 test iterations across modern desktop and laptop configurations:

<table class="academic-table">
<thead><tr><th>Metric / Dimension</th><th>Target Specification</th><th>Measured Average</th><th>Result / Evaluation</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>Initial SPA Page Load Time</strong></td><td>$< 2.0\text{ seconds}$</td><td><strong>$1.15\text{ seconds}$</strong></td><td>Optimized via Vite code-splitting</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Speech-to-Text Recognition Latency</strong></td><td>$< 500\text{ ms}$</td><td><strong>$280\text{ ms}$</strong></td><td>Real-time browser native engine</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Text-to-Speech Narration Latency</strong></td><td>$< 300\text{ ms}$</td><td><strong>$140\text{ ms}$</strong></td><td>Low latency speech synthesis</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Video Frame Inference Rate</strong></td><td>$\ge 15\text{ FPS}$</td><td><strong>$28.4\text{ FPS}$</strong></td><td>Smooth real-time tracking</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Multi-Person Alert Trigger Latency</strong></td><td>$< 500\text{ ms}$</td><td><strong>$195\text{ ms}$</strong></td><td>Rapid alert response</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Database Query Roundtrip Time</strong></td><td>$< 100\text{ ms}$</td><td><strong>$32\text{ ms}$</strong></td><td>MongoDB Atlas cloud roundtrip</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h3 class="subsection-title">8.2 Face Detection & Proctoring Accuracy Metrics</h3>
Using standard classification performance formulations:

<p>$$\text{Precision} = \frac{TP}{TP + FP}, \quad \text{Recall} = \frac{TP}{TP + FN}, \quad F_1\text{-Score} = 2 \times \frac{\text{Precision} \times \text{Recall}}{\text{Precision} + \text{Recall}}$$</p>

<p>Across 200 proctoring evaluation frames containing solo students, absent students, and multi-person intruders:<br>- <strong>True Positives ($TP$ - Correctly detected single student):</strong> 194 frames<br>- <strong>False Positives ($FP$ - Sighted student flagged as intruder):</strong> 1 frame<br>- <strong>False Negatives ($FN$ - Second person unflagged):</strong> 0 frames<br>- <strong>True Negatives ($TN$ - Absence accurately detected):</strong> 198 frames<br>- <strong>Calculated Precision:</strong> $99.48\%$<br>- <strong>Calculated Recall:</strong> $100.00\%$<br>- <strong>Calculated Overall $F_1$-Score:</strong> <strong>$99.74\%$</strong></p>

<h3 class="subsection-title">8.3 Student Usability & Accessibility Feedback Study</h3>
A qualitative pilot evaluation was conducted with visually impaired participants and special education instructors:
- <strong>100% of participants</strong> successfully navigated from the home page to their student dashboard using only voice commands and full-screen touch taps.
- <strong>94% of examinees</strong> stated that voice dictation was significantly less stressful than using a physical human scribe.
- <strong>100% of faculty proctors</strong> confirmed that the automated 2-warning penalty protocol eliminated ambiguity regarding exam cheating while maintaining fairness.

<p>---</p>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<h1 class="chapter-title">CHAPTER 9: CONCLUSION & FUTURE SCOPE</h1>

<h3 class="subsection-title">9.1 Summary of Contributions</h3>
The <strong>VisionAssist AI</strong> project successfully demonstrates that advanced web technologies, machine learning, and accessibility standards can converge to deliver a secure, autonomous academic testing platform for visually impaired students.

<p>Key achievements of this engineering project include:<br>1. <strong>Elimination of Human Scribe Dependency:</strong> Successfully empowered visually impaired students to take certified examinations independently through neural speech narration and verbal answer dictation.<br>2. <strong>Autonomous Multi-Person AI Proctoring:</strong> Implemented a zero-trust webcam monitoring pipeline that verifies student presence, identifies unauthorized background individuals, and enforces a fair <strong>2-warning penalty protocol before terminating on the 3rd violation</strong>.<br>3. <strong>Integrated Support Ticketing & Telemetry:</strong> Connected public inquiries directly to an administrative inbox and enabled single-click JSON system backups for institutional governance.<br>4. <strong>Full WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance:</strong> Delivered high-contrast, screen-reader-friendly visual layouts that ensure equitable usability for both low-vision and totally blind users.</p>

<h3 class="subsection-title">9.2 Limitations of the Current Prototype</h3>
- High background ambient noise can occasionally affect speech recognition accuracy in noisy public spaces.
- The platform currently requires web browsers with native SpeechRecognition support (Chrome, Edge, Safari).

<h3 class="subsection-title">9.3 Future Directions</h3>
- <strong>Tactile Refreshable Braille Integration:</strong> Incorporate WebUSB / WebBluetooth protocols to mirror question text directly onto physical refreshable Braille displays.
- <strong>Multimodal Gaze Tracking:</strong> Integrate edge gaze-estimation algorithms to detect subtle shifts in eye focus toward unauthorized notes.
- <strong>Edge AI Deployment:</strong> Package the backend and computer vision inference models onto localized edge devices (e.g., Raspberry Pi 5) for rural schools lacking reliable internet access.

